DHCPC(1)                     User Commands

NAME
    dhcpc - DHCP client

SYNOPSIS
    dhcpc [-i IF | -a] [-1] [-f] [-t SECONDS] [-s SERVER] [-p PORT]

DESCRIPTION
    Obtains an IPv4 address, netmask, gateway, name servers and domain
    name for IF (default eth0) with DHCP, configures the interface
    through /dev/net and writes /etc/resolv.conf, with the domain name
    as its search list. The lease is renewed at T1 by unicast to
    the server, rebound at T2 by broadcast, and removed at expiry, after
    which discovery starts again. Without a server the client retries
    with backoff from 4 to 64 seconds and leaves the interface without an
    address. A NAK removes the address at once.

    Without -1 or -f the client detaches and keeps running. -1 exits with
    status 0 after the first lease or 1 after SECONDS (default 60) without
    one. -f stays in the foreground. -s and -p send to a unicast test
    server instead of broadcasting to port 67.

    -a is the form init runs as the dhcp service: the interface comes
    from the first "iface NAME dhcp" line of /etc/network, the client
    stays in the foreground, and it exits with status 0 when the file
    has no such line or the interface is absent, so the service stops
    quietly on a machine without a network. initctl restart dhcp starts
    it again after /etc/network changed.

    Replies are accepted only for the client's transaction and MAC
    address, and only when they carry a subnet mask, server identifier
    and lease time of at least 10 seconds; anything else is ignored.

FILES
    /dev/net, /etc/resolv.conf

SEE ALSO
    net(1), init.conf(5), initctl(1), resolv.conf(5), index(7)
